Decorator -- takes another function as an argument, and replaces it. Decorator functions are executed immediately when a decorator module is loaded (at import time), but decorated functions run when they are explicitly invoked (at runtime)
-- can be nested and parametrized (decorator factory)

dis module -- disassembling bytecode

Closures -- function that can access nonglobal variables defined outside of its body (matters only when you have nested functions). Closure retains bindings to free variables that exist when the function is defined so that they can be used when the function is invoked and the defining scope is no longer available

free variable -- not bound in the local scope
nonlocal keyword -- allows to flag variable as free even when assigned within a function

functools.lru_cache() -- function memoization decorator
fuctools.singledispatch -- decorator to register specialized functions even for classes you cant edit
